# Lampose Partner (Food-Partner) — environment variables
# Copy to `.env` and fill in your own values. `.env` is gitignored.

# Backend API base URL. No trailing slash and no version suffix — the app
# appends the versioned paths itself. The one Lampose backend listens on 5001.
#
# LEAVE IT EMPTY to run the whole onboarding flow locally with no server: the
# application is logged to the console instead of posted, exactly as the
# website's food-partner module does today. There is no endpoint for it yet.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# Which build this is: development | preview | production.
#
# Decides whether the app narrates itself to the console (`lib/log.ts`) — off
# in production, since a fetch failure is logged with the error it came from,
# and that error can carry a restaurant's own orders and payout details.
#
# LEAVE IT EMPTY under Metro: it is inferred as development from `__DEV__`.
# A release build must set it to `production` explicitly — an unset value in
# a shipped build is also treated as production, so a forgotten variable
# fails safe rather than leaving logging on.
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=
